(footprint "RaspberryPi_5_GPIO_Socket_2x20"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Raspberry Pi 5 40-pin GPIO socket (female 2x20, 2.54mm) plus 4 non-plated M3 mounting holes 49 x 58 mm apart. MOUNTING: Pi sits ABOVE the carrier, upside down, so its male pins come down into this socket. COLUMN ORDER 2026-08-05: the EVEN row (2,4,...40, which carries both 5V pins) is the OUTBOARD column, away from the Pi body; the ODD row (1,3,...39, pin 1 = 3V3) is INBOARD. Set from the physical board by the builder - the two rows straddle the mounting-hole line, so this is order only, not position. This footprint has had a column transposition once before on V2. **CONTINUITY-CHECK pad 2 and pad 4 against 5V on a real Pi BEFORE applying power** - getting this backwards puts 5V onto Pi pin 1 (the 3V3 rail) and pin 3 (a GPIO) and destroys the Pi.")
	(tags "Through hole socket strip THT 2x20 2.54mm double row")
	(property "Reference" "J3"
		(at -1.27 -2.77 0)
